## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Defense-in-depth for Ctrl+C, not the fix itself (that was
## `Sprat.Terminal.Mode`'s `stty raw -echo` failing to reach the real tty
## — see that module's moduledoc for the actual root cause and how it's
## fixed). With `stty raw -echo` genuinely clearing ISIG, the kernel never
## turns Ctrl+C into a real SIGINT in the first place, so `erl`'s own
## break handler never triggers regardless of this flag — confirmed via a
## real tmux capture with `vm.args` empty (no BREAK menu, Ctrl+C reaches
## `Sprat.Terminal.Keybindings` normally). `+Bi` ("ignore break") is kept
## anyway as a backstop: if ISIG ever fails to clear for some other reason
## (the exact failure mode this bug started as), a real SIGINT still
## reaches `erl`, and without this flag `erl` defaults to `+Bc` — the
## original bug's "BREAK: (a)bort ..." menu, then VM death on a second
## Ctrl+C. `+Bi` degrades that same failure to merely-inert instead of
## destructive. `+Bd` (docs/phase0/03-terminal-spike.md) was tried first
## and is worse here: no menu, but it kills the VM outright on the first
## Ctrl+C rather than asking.
+Bi

## Increase number of concurrent ports/sockets
##+Q 65536

## Tweak GC to run more often
##-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## Enable deployment without epmd
## (requires changing both vm.args and remote.vm.args)
##-start_epmd false -erl_epmd_port 6789
